WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.435
-You know, it's important
to remember

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.170
there are two sides
to every news story.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.640
To make sure you get to see
important issues from all sides,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.041
we've invited two of
our writers who have

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.409
very different points of view.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.611
We will examine their opinions
in a segment we call

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.480
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.083
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.153 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.855
I'm joined by Ally and Amber.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.189
Thank you so much for
being here today.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.890
First topic...

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.694 line:0%
it seems that every day that
someone within Trump's world

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.896 line:0%
resigns or is fired.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:32.531 line:0%
Is this a sign of house
in chaos,

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.300 line:0%
or that President Trump finally
seems to know

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.702 line:0%
the kind of team he needs? Ally?

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:37.937
-You're giving him
too much credit.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.905
All this turnover isn't
calculated.

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:42.041
It's the tantrums
of a man-child.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.409
It's like if
a middle school bully

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.511
tried to run a PTA meeting.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.747
Trump is nothing
but a big, fat baby.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.548
-A big, fat baby? Amber?

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:53.152
-I love, big, fat babies.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:56.389
You see one, and you ask,
"How did you get so fat

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.857
if all you eat is milk,
little baby?"

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:01.727
But they don't answer because
they're a baby.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:04.430
And when they're real fat,
you get to put your finger

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.165
on their chin and go...

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.935
[ Imitating Fat Albert ]
Hey, hey, hey, it's Fat Albert.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.637
It's the cutest!

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:14.040
-You do have an excellent point.
Next topic...

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.243 line:0%
Trump issued a memorandum
banning transgender people

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.677 line:0%
from serving in the military

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.313 line:0%
except under
limited circumstances.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.683 line:0%
Is this a dead end cause
or a win for his base? Ally?

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.885
-It's another sideshow.
I mean, think about it.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.119
Right before
a national gun march

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:29.088
and a TV interview
with one of his mistresses,

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.690
Trump releases a hateful policy
to grab headlines.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.559
The courts will hopefully
fight this,

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:36.429
but I think it's another one of
Trump's distracting stunts.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.264
-Distracting stunts. Amber?

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.467
-I love stunts.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.136
You'll be watching a movie,
and then the music will start

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.471
to get tense, like...
[ Hums tense theme ]

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.840
And then the actors
will punch each other

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.942
and break everything
and fly through walls,

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.145
and then at some point,
you'll be, like, "Wait,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.414
that's not the actor.
That's a stuntman."

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:57.483
Then the actor reappears
and says a cool line like...

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.751
[ Deep voice ]
"I thought I might as well

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.919
take a stab at it."
[ Normal voice ] And you're

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.056
like, that's cool because
he stabbed him.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.256
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:06.292
-Seth, what she's saying
is completely off-topic.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.895
-Ally, it's called
"Point, Counterpoint."

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:11.197
You make a point.
She makes a counterpoint.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.898
-The Pope was wrong.
Hell is real.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:14.767
[ Laughter ]
-Ally.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.937
-Ally, don't be sad.
Put a grin on your chin,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.874
open your arms,
and bring it in!

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:22.842
-Absolutely not. Next topic.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.845 line:0%
-Finally, after Joe Biden
said in his speech he would

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.946 line:0%
have beat Trump up
in high school,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.714 line:0%
Trump tweeted
that if they did fight,

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:30.416 line:0%
Biden would have gone down
hard and fast,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.519 line:0%
while crying ahead
of the midterms.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.588 line:0%
Is this the sort of leadership
we need from either party? Ally.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.356
-It's like
we've completely forgotten

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:39.058
how a leader
is supposed to act.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.028
This country has gone insane.
I've lost all hope.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.764
-I know what would make
you feel better.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.699
-I'm not giving you a hug.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:51.437
-Oh. Well, then how
about a big stunt sequence?

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.973
-You mean it?
-Yeah. Go nuts.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:58.044
[ Action movie music playing ]
Aah! Uhh!

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:01.313
-[ Whimpers ] Uhh!

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:05.051
Aah! Oh!

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.253 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:11.190
-[ Grunting ]

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.892
[ Glass shatters ]

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.729
[ Grunting ]

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.165 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:22.034
[ Grunting ]

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.869
-[ Audience groans ]

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.639
-Hey, you, two, knock it off!

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:30.009
-Take a closer look at this,
bitch!

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:34.147
-Uhh! Oh, no!

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.047
-Aah!
-Say it!

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:36.182
-No!
-Say it!

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.283
-No!
-Say it!

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.918
-Okay, fine.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.553
Give me a hug.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.455
-Okay.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.856
[ Applause ]

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.759
-This has been "Point...
[ Groans ] Counterpoint."

